{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":19313,"name":"Viniciuserra","username":"viniciuserra","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/v/258eb7/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-04T15:38:32.965Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi organizers,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rules state that external data and pre-trained models are allowed, but that\u003cbr\u003e\nfor prize eligibility external data must be “freely and publicly available to all\u003cbr\u003e\nparticipants” and licensed to permit commercial use (no NC / CC NC / CC BY-NC).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d like to confirm how this applies to \u003cstrong\u003ePPMI\u003c/strong\u003e (Parkinson’s Progression Markers\u003cbr\u003e\nInitiative, ida.loni.usc.edu), which is the largest public DaT-SPECT collection\u003cbr\u003e\nand the obvious external candidate for this task. Its access model is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFree of charge and open to any researcher — no fee, no selection committee for\u003cbr\u003e\nthe standard tiers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBut \u003cstrong\u003egated\u003c/strong\u003e: you must register with LONI IDA and sign a Data Use Agreement\u003cbr\u003e\nbefore downloading.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe DUA restricts redistribution (data may not be shared beyond the\u003cbr\u003e\ninvestigators named in the request), limits use to the purpose described in the\u003cbr\u003e\napplication, and attaches IP policies.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo PPMI is “freely available to anyone who applies”, but it is not downloadable\u003cbr\u003e\nwithout an individual agreement and it is not released under an open license in\u003cbr\u003e\nthe CC/MIT sense. That seems to sit right on the boundary of the rule, hence the\u003cbr\u003e\nquestion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpecifically:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDoes PPMI satisfy “freely and publicly available to all participants” for\u003cbr\u003e\nprize eligibility, given the registration + DUA gate?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDoes the DUA’s purpose-limitation and no-redistribution clause conflict with\u003cbr\u003e\nthe commercial-use requirement?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDoes the same answer apply to \u003cstrong\u003eweights pretrained on PPMI\u003c/strong\u003e — either trained\u003cbr\u003e\nby me, or third-party released checkpoints? Is a model derived from DUA-gated\u003cbr\u003e\ndata treated like the data itself?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf PPMI is not eligible, is it still permitted for non-prize-eligible\u003cbr\u003e\nsubmissions or for methodological exploration, provided the final submitted\u003cbr\u003e\nmodel is trained only on challenge data?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe same question applies to other DaT datasets released under “academic use\u003cbr\u003e\nonly” terms, such as the NTUA Parkinson dataset.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClarifying this early would help a lot with planning. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-04T20:19:49.167Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":21,"readers_count":20,"score":24.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":11472,"topic_slug":"is-ppmi-dua-gated-acceptable-as-external-data-for-prize-eligibility","display_username":"Viniciuserra","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":7461,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/is-ppmi-dua-gated-acceptable-as-external-data-for-prize-eligibility/11472/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":19321,"name":"Mdaley","username":"mdaley","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a3d4f5/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-05T14:19:22.088Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHello,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreat question! The DUA states that “any model that has been trained using participant-level data may only be shared through MJFF-approved methods,” and it grants access to the data “for the purpose of scientific investigation, teaching, or the planning of clinical research studies.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause competition use doesn’t fall under those purposes, and because winning models must be openly licensed for commercial use, models trained on this data wouldn’t be eligible for prizes.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-05T14:19:22.088Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":19,"readers_count":18,"score":18.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":11472,"topic_slug":"is-ppmi-dua-gated-acceptable-as-external-data-for-prize-eligibility","display_username":"Mdaley","primary_group_name":"drivendata-staff","flair_name":"drivendata-staff","flair_url":"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex028/uploads/drivendata1/original/2X/c/ccc07e6a647e62601ee79f5014eac0f94bc81547.png","flair_bg_color":"efefef","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"DrivenData Staff","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":7213,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_ur